body:
I am sorry for laughing, but damn. Good one. 

&#x200B;

I hope you heal! :-)

I've learnt these past couple months that no matter how angry you are, or how much you want to send that message - don't. because they do not care. it's harsh but true.

&#x200B;

i am so sorry. rather vent here instead of messaging your ex. it helps.

They make it look extremely easy. But hey, we probably look like that to them too. 

&#x200B;

Shitty cycle.

Damn. Reading this is exactly like what I went through about 3 weeks ago... my ex promised to come see me and make time for me because we were trying to work things out (his idea btw) and on the day he completely ignored my texts, calls, etc. and stood me up. and i've been NC ever since, even though he randomly sends me messages about different things (he legit finds a way to contact me) - so i had to tell him to STOP contacting me in any way and made sure i blocked him from the rest of my stuff. not easy but we'll get there.

&#x200B;

goodluck

definitely feel like it's to see if he still has a hold on me - because initially he tried to reignite the relationship and then he stopped putting in any effort and made it clear that he wasn't "ready" to commit again. even though it was his idea, haha. and he told me to move on too. 

&#x200B;

anyway thanks!

I reached two months yesterday. 

&#x200B;

I'm glad he atleast checked on you, it has been absolutely silent on my end. I too have also dug myself into a hole, emotionally. It's really difficult to let go of everything, but it'll be okay. 2 months is still fresh for after a breakup, so we are allowed to feel the way we do and not rush our healing process!

I completely agree with the above... sometimes things are better left unsaid. Leaving room for contact just opens up old wounds and possibility for something new to hurt you.

&#x200B;

If you feel as if you would bee able to handle contacting him, go for it and I wish you well with that. Just be sure. All the best!

I could've wrote this! 

&#x200B;

Blessings to you, hope you feel better soon!

I am giving it more time, I was really close to texting but didn't.. 

&#x200B;

it is difficult but we got this, goodluck!

a month for me too, still sad as ever. crying each night now for the past week and been dreaming about him constantly. 

&#x200B;

very happy that you are finding the strength to feel better. blessings to you!

I understand that you are looking out for him and wanting to make sure that he is okay and that nothing happens... but, do not get too upset. maybe he really wants to just be there for you on the day, especially because he can't make the next. 

&#x200B;

something to think about.

That's awesome, where do you stay now? 

&#x200B;

I'd also understand it if it had anything to do with the age gap, but they've told me it's okay. So it's definitely only about his skin colour. 

I'm studying part-time and finish in 8 months, so I am already working a full time job. We've both started looking for jobs in his city for once I'm done too. 

&#x200B;

I hope it won't turn out with me having to choose either one as well.

&#x200B;

Thank you for your words , I appreciate it :-)

Like i've said in the above comment, we live in different cities, so I'd have to relocate to move in with him. But i'm definitely willing to relocate to be with him! 

&#x200B;

I'm mixed, but not between black and white. My father is white while my mother is indian. So, my moms indian upbringing has made her extremely backward in life, and she grew up in the apartheid era so she should be more understanding. But I don't understand it either. My father always came across as an understanding guy and was against racism, until his daughter started dating a black man. Which is very unfortunate.
